            <ArticleTitle>Postoperative analgesia in dental day case surgery. A comparison between Feldene &quot;Melt' (piroxicam) and diclofenac suppositories.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>784-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A randomised, double-blind placebo-controlled trial was conducted to compare the analgesic efficacy of piroxicam as Feldene &quot;Melt' with diclofenac suppositories following day case wisdom tooth extraction. Piroxicam was found to be equivalent to diclofenac in speed of onset and efficacy when given 1 h prior to surgery with no significant adverse effects. It is therefore possible to confer the benefits of postoperative analgesia from a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug whilst avoiding the inconvenience of the rectal route of administration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
